   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "response = llm.invoke(\"Could you explain what is Agentic AI in simple terms?\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "id": "63ffc2b5",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Agentic AI refers to a type of artificial intelligence (AI) that can make decisions and take actions on its own, without being explicitly programmed or controlled by humans. The term \"agentic\" comes from the concept of agency, which means having the ability to act intentionally and make choices.\n",
      "\n",
      "In simple terms, Agentic AI is like a self-aware agent that can:\n",
      "\n",
      "1. Learn from experience\n",
      "2. Make decisions based on its own understanding of the world\n",
      "3. Take actions to achieve its goals\n",
      "\n",
      "Agentic AI systems are designed to be autonomous, flexible, and adaptable, allowing them to navigate complex environments and interact with humans in a more natural way.\n",
      "\n",
      "Think of it like a highly advanced robot that can:\n",
      "\n",
      "* Learn from trial and error\n",
      "* Adjust its behavior based on new information\n",
      "* Make decisions without being explicitly told what to do\n",
      "\n",
      "Agentic AI has the potential to revolutionize various fields, such as healthcare, finance, and transportation, by enabling systems to learn, adapt, and make decisions autonomously.\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "print(response.content)"
   ]
